{"id": "K122", "tool": "retract_claim", "args": {"claim": "C5", "reason": "Referee: compared different nights (ATE's off-minimum nights pulled V shallow). Same-night depths are B 1.49, V 1.44, I 1.23 and the colour slopes match 2014 (see referee claim C15)."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T09:00:56+00:00", "oddsky": "0.2.0"}
{"id": "K123", "tool": "retract_claim", "args": {"claim": "C6", "reason": "Referee: single faintest points inflate depths (2014 visual faintest gives 1.0 vs 0.70 from medians). Superseded by the referee's median-based history (C16, C17)."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T09:00:56+00:00", "oddsky": "0.2.0"}
{"id": "K124", "tool": "retract_claim", "args": {"claim": "C9", "reason": "Referee: a SIMBAD title check of the 25 most recent references is not a novelty check. Both eclipses were professional-led AAVSO campaigns (Alert Notice 700, Campaign #894) with publication planned."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T09:00:56+00:00", "oddsky": "0.2.0"}
{"id": "K125", "tool": "retract_claim", "args": {"claim": "C8", "reason": "Overstated as an inference: precession is an existing published interpretation whose model predicted ~2.0 mag for 2014 (observed 0.71), and the 2014/2025 shapes differ. Restated as speculation in a new claim."}, "digest": "6bc0da1f42f96fc3", "author": "claude-opus-5.5", "at": "2026-10-27T09:00:56+00:00", "oddsky": "0.2.0"}
